.TH LOGICFORGE 1 "" "LogicForge @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
logicforge \- digital logic simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logicforge
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B logicforge
starts the LogicForge workbench, a graphical editor and simulator for digital logic
circuits with four-state signals, hierarchical subcircuits, physical 7400-series chips,
a logic analyzer and the programmable LF-8 computer.
.PP
If \fIFILE\fR is given, that LogicForge project (\fI.logic\fR) is opened. A file that
cannot be read is reported in a dialog; the workbench still starts. Only one project is
opened per window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/logicforge/logicforge.log
Log of unexpected errors (default \fI~/.local/state/logicforge/logicforge.log\fR).
Nothing is ever sent anywhere.
.TP
.I PROJECT.logic.bak
The previous version of a project, kept next to it whenever LogicForge saves.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the user interface could not be started, 2 for invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home: https://github.com/MichaelWeissDEV/LogicForge
